%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:backup@

%9Parameters:%9

    NOW:         Makes a backup now, into backup_dir, also when
                 backup_auto is off, and says how it went.

    Without an argument: whether automatic backups are on, where they
    go and how many are kept, when the last one was made and its file,
    why the last try failed, and when the next one is due.

%9Description:%9

    Backs up the erssi home (config, themes, scripts, the E2E keyring,
    OTR and fe-web keys, credentials and the Mentions log; not the IRC
    logs) into one file, the same backup as erssi --backup FILE. erssi
    runs the installer that was installed with it
    (shellter-install.sh --backup) in the background, so erssi goes on
    while it runs; one backup runs at a time.

    The file is backup_dir/erssi-auto-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.tar.gz, of mode
    0600: it holds your private keys and passwords, so keep it private.
    After each backup the newest backup_keep files of that name are kept
    and older ones removed; other files in backup_dir are never touched.
    Restore one from a shell with erssi --restore FILE.

    erssi backs up by itself only with backup_auto daily or weekly
    (/HELP backup_auto). An erssi that the installer did not install has
    nothing to run, and in Capsicum capability mode no program can be
    started; /BACKUP says why.

%9Examples:%9

    /BACKUP
    /BACKUP NOW
    /SET backup_auto daily

%9See also:%9 BACKUP_AUTO, BACKUP_DIR, BACKUP_KEEP
